From: pmos-munch bring-up <bringup@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: qcom: rpmhpd: select PM_OPP

RPMh domains implement set_performance_state. The genpd provider registers
an indexed OPP table for these domains. Without PM_OPP the OPP stub returns
-EOPNOTSUPP and of_genpd_add_provider_onecell() fails with -95.

Observed on munch with the minimal allnoconfig profile. Express the missing
framework dependency rather than deleting CPU/apps_rsc power-domain links.
This patch changes no hardware voltages, clocks or DT properties directly;
successful probe permits the existing genpd topology to become functional.

--- a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/Kconfig
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 config QCOM_RPMHPD
 	tristate "Qualcomm RPMh Power domain driver"
 	depends on QCOM_RPMH && QCOM_COMMAND_DB
+	select PM_OPP
 	help
 	  QCOM RPMh Power domain driver to support power-domains with
 	  performance states. The driver communicates a performance state
